Recommended execution order

This sequence validates the complete lifecycle:

1. ✅ Create Work Order
2. ✅ Get Work Order
3. ✅ List Work Orders
4. ✅ Update → In Progress
5. ✅ Get Dispatch Logs
6. ✅ Update → Completed
7. ✅ Get Dispatch Logs Again
8. ✅ Create Second Work Order
9. ✅ Cancel Second Work Order
10. ✅ Invalid Work Order
11. ✅ Invalid Status Update

This is the same style of end-to-end validation we used for the Settlement and Reserve agents: you verify the agent chooses the correct MCP tool, then confirm the corresponding changes (or lack of changes) in work_orders and dispatch_logs after each step.
